- op: discuss  # a18a
  at: '2026-08-12T23:21:34Z'  # a18a
  by: agent  # a18a
  actor: jgstern_agent  # a18a
  clock: 3  # a18a
  nonce: a18a  # a18a
  message: "Observed while running check-package-coverage for the INV-dabov PR; re-run with no edits passed all six packages, and the test passes standalone. Filed rather than folded into that PR: it is tracker-package test infrastructure, unrelated to the verify-claims change, and a security fix should not carry an unrelated gate tweak."  # a18a
- op: discuss  # 45f2
  at: '2026-10-01T03:33:56Z'  # 45f2
  by: agent  # 45f2
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 45f2
  clock: 4  # 45f2
  nonce: 45f2  # 45f2
  message: "BEARS ON THIS ROW (from WI-ruhul-kujah-sasar-mofov-mohoh-gotis-soron-fazun, branch jgstern-agent/fix/ruhul, local, not merged):\n\nDirection (b) is built for the tracker package's four properties: packages/hypergumbo-tracker/tests/test_compile_properties.py now applies one shared `settings(max_examples=50, deadline=None, suppress_health_check=[HealthCheck.too_slow])` to test_idempotency, test_permutation_invariance, test_created_at_always_set and test_updated_at_gte_created_at.\n\nBehavioral pin, not a syntactic one: TestPropertiesSurviveASlowExample patches the module's compile_ops to sleep 0.3 s on its FIRST call only, then calls each property. Before the change, all four failed with FlakyFailure wrapping DeadlineExceeded (\"Falsified on the first call but did not on a subsequent one\"), which is this row's mechanism exactly; after it, all four pass.\n\nNOT COVERED, still exposed: tests/test_transcript_pipeline_properties.py (5 properties at lines ~118-216, `@settings(max_examples=50)`, no deadline=). No `register_profile` exists in the repo, so direction (a) is still unbuilt. This row's own test_idempotency observation is plausibly what WI-ruhul's 08-21 discussion recorded (the failure messages there were not kept)."  # 45f2
- op: discuss  # f2fa
  at: '2026-10-03T09:18:10Z'  # f2fa
  by: agent  # f2fa
  actor: jgstern_agent  # f2fa
  clock: 5  # f2fa
  nonce: f2fa  # f2fa
  message: "SIBLING MECHANISM, 2026-10-03: the same parallel-load flake also fires through Hypothesis's HealthCheck.too_slow, not only the 200ms deadline. tests/test_transcript_pipeline_properties.py::TestFilterNewLines::test_output_never_exceeds_input failed twice today under board load (\"Input generation is slow: Hypothesis only generated 7 valid inputs after 1.60 seconds\"; one draw 1.592 s): once in the WI-kabaf agent's targeted run and once in the stage-1 integration run (1 failed / 11487 passed, 463 files at 3 CPUs beside another smart-test). Re-run alone it passed (51 passed in 8.02s). A fix for this item should cover too_slow as well as the deadline (e.g. a profile that suppresses both under parallel runs), or name it as out of scope."  # f2fa
- op: discuss  # 28f0
  at: '2026-11-01T10:55:45Z'  # 28f0
  by: agent  # 28f0
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 28f0
  clock: 6  # 28f0
  nonce: 28f0  # 28f0
  message: "P3 REVIEW 2026-11-01 (dev 100b6fbb6e; owner-requested re-check of open P3 items last modified before 2026-10-20; fixtures under ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/p3_review_11012026/tool1/). VERDICT: PARTLY-STALE. At dev 100b6fbb6e the tracker half is fixed: test_compile_properties.py:173 has a shared settings(deadline=None, suppress too_slow) plus a slow-example pin, merged in c38b7a63a8. Still exposed: tests/test_transcript_pipeline_properties.py has 9 @settings(max_examples=50) with no deadline and no HealthCheck suppression, and the repo has no register_profile. The remaining scope is that file plus a global profile covering deadline and too_slow. MECHANISM: property tests inherit Hypothesis default per-example deadline and too_slow health check, so a timing check reports as a correctness failure under load. SHARES MECHANISM WITH: WI-narum."  # 28f0
